{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-343977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(4.9)=3.12$ and $f(5.1)=2.36,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(5).$\n\n${f}^{′}(5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-343977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=5$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(5) & ≈\\frac{f(5+0.1)-f(5-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5.1)-f(4.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.36-3.12}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-0.76)}{0.2} \\\\  & =-3.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-343977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-343977" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-343977" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3.8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-75121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(9.6)=3$ and $f(10.4)=11,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(10).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-75121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=10$ with the step size $h=0.4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(10) & ≈\\frac{f(10+0.4)-f(10-0.4)}{2(0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(10.4)-f(9.6)}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{11-3}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{0.8} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-75121" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-75121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-75121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11.5"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-75121" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(2.9)=5.91$ and $f(3.1)=7.11,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=3$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{f(3+0.1)-f(3-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3.1)-f(2.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7.11-5.91}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.2}{0.2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-170649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5.2"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "6.8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-343970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-5.0$ | $-4.0$ | $-2.7$ | $-1.0$ | $0.5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation.\n\n${g}^{′}(-1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-343970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{g(-1+1)-g(-1-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(0)-g(-2)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.0-(-4.0)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-343970" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-343970" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-343970" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-32535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-1.05$ | $-1$ | $-0.95$ | $-0.9$ | $-0.85$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $3.4$ | $2.5$ | $1.6$ | $2.1$ | $2.7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-32535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.05.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{g(-1+0.05)-g(-1-0.05)}{2(0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(-0.95)-g(-1.05)}{2(0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.6-3.4}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1.8}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18}{1} \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-32535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-32535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-32535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{g}^{′}(-1)≈-16"] ["math" "{g}^{′}(-1)≈-17"] ["math" "{g}^{′}(-1)≈-18"] ["math" "{g}^{′}(-1)≈-20"] ["math" "{g}^{′}(-1)≈-22"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-32535" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{g}^{′}(-1)≈-18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/85aff149fcbad4437f64f7d6eab96a42a287417c6c8f5483a03bf6fc2f22b930.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+1)-g(4-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(5)-g(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170650" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-170650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.5"] ["math" "0.75"] ["math" "0.8"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "1.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170650" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/e4097b002333ba5b874632c61ecbb2b212235a1cc74912b2f74bcb5740e86e02.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=3$ and $x=5.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(4)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{f(4+1)-f(4-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(5)-f(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-(-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-344027" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344027" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/ab10c9d133e6a383439b0a8b89643564f5f438d061dba647288927102e870a1b.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=-1$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=2.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=-3$ and $x=1.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(-1)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=-1$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & ≈\\frac{f(-1+2)-f(-1-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1)-f(-3)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)}{4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-344006" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344006" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/28cef739fd66e414894e830a02582f979dfdf285b3208cff5bba42b68537eefa.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=8$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=2.$\n\n*Hint: Assume that the graph passes through the points with integer $y$-coordinates when $x=6$ and $x=10.$*\n\n${f}^{′}(8)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=8$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(8) & ≈\\frac{f(8+2)-f(8-2)}{2(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(10)-f(6)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2-2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)}{4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344341" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-344341" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344341" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/7f36258f966a7af5ae9f35c4e3214bb8c2c7d0ae66039256b2484df5b34d83fb.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat the point $x=3$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{g(3+1)-g(3-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(4)-g(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-4}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-170651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-1.5"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-2.5"] ["math" "-3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-170651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-47504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The temperature of a certain liquid under heating is given by the function $T(t),$ where $t$ is the time in hours. The values of $T(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1.2$ | $1.4$ | $1.6$ | $1.8$ | $2.0$ | $2.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T(t)$ | $-12$ | $-10$ | $-4$ | $6$ | $10$ | $13$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nDetermine the instantaneous temperature rate at the instant of time $t=1.6$ using a central difference approximation with the step size $h=0.2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-47504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{T}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{T(t+h)-T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=1.6$ with step size $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(1.6) & ≈\\frac{T(1.6+0.2)-T(1.6-0.2)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(1.8)-T(1.4)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-(-10)}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{0.4} \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous temperature rate at the instant of time $t=1.6$ is ${40}^{∘}$ per hour." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-47504" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-47504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-47504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${16}^{∘}$ per hour"] ["text" "${20}^{∘}$ per hour"] ["text" "${40}^{∘}$ per hour"] ["text" "${4}^{∘}$ per hour"] ["text" "${8}^{∘}$ per hour"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-47504" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${40}^{∘}$ per hour"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-51402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Sam wanted to estimate the rate of weight growth of his new puppy. He took note of its weight every week, for $7$ weeks. The results are shown in the table below, where $W(t)$ is the puppy's weight (measured in pounds) after $t$ weeks from birth.\n\n| **$t$** | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $W(t)$ | $9$ | $10.1$ | $11.3$ | $12.4$ | $13.5$ | $14.6$ | $15.8$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the puppy's rate of weight growth $12$ weeks after birth using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-51402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{W(t+h)-W(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \nat the time $t=12$ and step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(0.2) & ≈\\frac{W(12+1)-W(12-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{W(13)-W(11)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14.6-12.4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2.2}{2} \\\\  & =1.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the rate of weight growth at the instant of time $t=12$ is $1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-51402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-51402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-51402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.05\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}"] ["math" "1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}"] ["math" "1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}"] ["math" "2.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}"] ["math" "2.2\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-51402" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.1\\,\\text{lb}/\\text{week}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In an environmental study, the water level in a reservoir (in $m$) after $t$ hours is given by the function $W(t).$ The values of $W(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $0.8$ | $1.0$ | $1.2$ | $1.4$ | $1.6$ | $1.8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$W(t)$** | $5.6$ | $5.3$ | $5.0$ | $4.7$ | $4.2$ | $3.9$ |\n\nApproximate the reservoir’s water level's instantaneous rate of change at $t=1.4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.2.$\n\nThe reservoir’s water level at $t=1.4$ is decreasing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $m$ per hour." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{W(t+h)-W(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=1.4$ with step size $h=0.2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′}(1.4) & ≈\\frac{W(1.4+0.2)-W(1.4-0.2)}{2(0.2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{W(1.6)-W(1.2)}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4.2-5.0}{0.4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-0.8}{0.4} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the reservoir’s water level at $t=1.4$ is decreasing at approximately $2\\,m$ per hour." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-344357" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344357" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a medical study, the concentration of a drug in a patient’s bloodstream (in $mg/L$) after $t$ hours is given by the function $C(t).$ The values of $C(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $2.0$ | $2.4$ | $2.8$ | $3.2$ | $3.6$ | $4.0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$C(t)$** | $12.4$ | $11.8$ | $11.0$ | $10.4$ | $9.8$ | $9.2$ |\n\nApproximate the drug’s concentration instantaneous rate of change at $t=3.2$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.4.$\n\nThe drug’s concentration at $t=3.2$ is decreasing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $mg/L$ per hour." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{C}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{C(t+h)-C(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=3.2$ with step size $h=0.4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(3.2) & ≈\\frac{C(3.2+0.4)-C(3.2-0.4)}{2(0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{C(3.6)-C(2.8)}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9.8-11.0}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1.2)}{0.8} \\\\  & =-1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the drug’s concentration at $t=3.2$ is decreasing at approximately $1.5\\,mg/L$ per hour." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344361" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-344361" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-344361" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-315235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In a lab experiment, the temperature of a chemical reactor (in ${}^{∘}C$) after $t$ minutes is given by the function $T(t).$ The values of $T(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $1.2$ | $1.6$ | $2.0$ | $2.4$ | $2.8$ | $3.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$T(t)$** | $28$ | $30$ | $32$ | $34$ | $35$ | $36$ |\n\nApproximate the reactor’s temperature instantaneous rate of change at $t=2.0$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.4.$\n\nThe reactor’s temperature at $t=2.0$ is changing at approximately \n{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}C$ per minute." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-315235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{T}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{T(t+h)-T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\nat time $t=2.0$ with step size $h=0.4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(2.0) & ≈\\frac{T(2.0+0.4)-T(2.0-0.4)}{2(0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(2.4)-T(1.6)}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{34-30}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{0.8} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the reactor’s temperature at $t=2.0$ is changing at approximately $5\\,{}^{∘}C$ per minute." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-315235" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "29e23e5fec80794cb7314cb5ad56b3cd69815efe28898490321d3c1d48b7493b"} {"question" "q-315235" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "q-315235" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/state.json" "file_sha256" "fc027076d5db14c7b261492d31e8751dd41f2e09127585459699af17e6669304"} {"question" "e-158" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $1.1$ | $1.3$ | $1.7$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate $f'(x)$ at the point $x=0.2$ using a central difference approximation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/example-158.json" "file_sha256" "d25e91b9adbd16ed778235055173c433fe12425ab6cd8d0eb7201a9d148285b2"} {"question" "e-158" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=0.2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0.2) & ≈\\frac{f(0.2+0.1)-f(0.2-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0.3)-f(0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.7-1.1}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.6}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/example-158.json" "file_sha256" "d25e91b9adbd16ed778235055173c433fe12425ab6cd8d0eb7201a9d148285b2"} {"question" "e-159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/5355859a0307e46ae84d12bc5e0b183d72458972c8a417fb6d9296b4769ea078.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/example-159.json" "file_sha256" "759a6e7da23c979ed1418c5f06b45c2b9f2c2fffa6285bca48f7eaaed43f130f"} {"question" "e-159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{g(x+h) - g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+4)-g(4-4)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(8)-g(0)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-(-10)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/example-159.json" "file_sha256" "759a6e7da23c979ed1418c5f06b45c2b9f2c2fffa6285bca48f7eaaed43f130f"} {"question" "e-160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A car engine is being heated from a temperature of about $-10^{\\circ}.$ The temperature of the engine after $t$ minutes is given by $T(t).$  The graph of $T(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/assets/fe78a78911e2df9cdb488ec57b0e0a34bb56e18b57303d895dc8013b64a4afc3.png)\n\nApproximate the rate at which the temperature of the engine increases when $t = 3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/example-160.json" "file_sha256" "b9cba1b00b4094e5af283d13133e9056d231f572d1f5dd92afec8edca0fb8896"} {"question" "e-160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nT'(t) \\approx \\dfrac{T(t+h) - T(t-h)}{2h},\n$$\n\n \n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{T(3+1)-T(3-1)}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{T(4)-T(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{60-30}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of temperature increase is approximately $15^{\\circ}$ per minute." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059223/example-160.json" "file_sha256" "b9cba1b00b4094e5af283d13133e9056d231f572d1f5dd92afec8edca0fb8896"}] "usage" {"q-32535" [] "e-158" [] "e-160" [] "e-159" []} "basis" 1887 "retractions" [[17592186078783 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nA function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $-1.05$ | $-1$ | $-0.95$ | $-0.9$ | $-0.85$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $g(x)$ | $3.4$ | $2.5$ | $1.6$ | $2.1$ | $2.7$ |\n\nApproximate $g^{′}(x)$ at the point $x =-1$ using a central difference approximation."] [17592186078129 :question/problem "A function $f(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $f(x)$ | $1$ | $1.1$ | $1.3$ | $1.7$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate $f'(x)$ at the point $x=0.2$ using a central difference approximation."] [17592186078129 :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nf'(x) \\approx \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.2$. We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1$. This gives\n\n$$\nf^{′}(0.2) \\mid \\approx (f(0.2 + 0.1) - f(0.2 - 0.1))/(2(0.1)); = (f(0.3) - f(0.1))/(2(0.1)); = \\frac{1.7 - 1.1}{0.2}; = \\frac{0.6}{0.2}; = \\frac{6}{2}; = 3\n$$"] [17592186078130 :question/problem "The graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above.\nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/640/Source/Images/a750fcfca1b253b803c467e2619376fd.png)"] [17592186078130 :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{g(x+h) - g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=4$. This gives\n\n$$\ng^{′}(4) \\mid \\approx (g(4 + 4) - g(4 - 4))/(2(4)); = (g(8) - g(0))/(8); = (-4 - (-10))/(8); = \\frac{6}{8}; = 0.75\n$$"] [17592186078133 :question/problem "A car engine is being heated from a temperature of about $-10^{\\circ}$. The temperature of the engine after $t$ minutes is given by $T(t)$. The graph of $T(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/640/Source/Images/2189fc374802d088f3c8ca4094372036.png)\n\nApproximate the rate at which the temperature of the engine increases when $t = 3$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=1$."] [17592186078133 :question/worked-solution "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\nT'(t) \\approx \\dfrac{T(t+h) - T(t-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=1$. This gives\n\n$$\nT^{′}(3) \\mid \\approx (T(3 + 1) - T(3 - 1))/(2(1)); = (T(4) - T(2))/(2); = \\frac{60 - 30}{2}; = \\frac{30}{2}; = 15\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of temperature increase is approximately $15^{\\circ}$ per minute."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186075915 17592186075916 17592186075917 17592186075918 17592186075919] "immutable_fields" [[17592186075914 :answer-field/correct] [17592186075914 :answer-field/id] [17592186075914 :answer-field/key] [17592186075914 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
